# Memory Map

## Memory Configuration
The memory configuration is defined in [src/memory.cfg](mdc:src/memory.cfg):

```asm
MEMORY {
    ZP:      start = $0000, size = $0100, type = rw;  // Zero Page
    STACK:   start = $0100, size = $0100, type = rw;  // Stack
    RAM:     start = $0200, size = $FD00, type = rw;  // Main RAM
    VECTORS: start = $FFFA, size = $0006, type = ro;  // Interrupt vectors
}
```

## Address Decoder
The [rtl/addressdecoder.sv](mdc:rtl/addressdecoder.sv) implements the memory mapping logic:

```systemverilog
// Memory Map Regions
// 0x0000-0x00FF: Zero Page
// 0x0100-0x01FF: Stack
// 0x0200-0x0FFF: Main RAM
// 0x1000-0x1FFF: Text buffer
// 0x2000-0x2FFF: Sprite memory
// 0x3000-0x3FFF: I/O space
// 0x4000-0x4FFF: Memory-mapped I/O
// 0xFFFA-0xFFFF: Interrupt vectors
```

## Interrupt Vectors
- NMI Vector: $FFFA-$FFFB
- Reset Vector: $FFFC-$FFFD
- IRQ/BRK Vector: $FFFE-$FFFF

## Program Starting Point
The program typically starts at $0300, as set by the reset vector in the ROM.
